WEBVTT

1
00:00:09.470 --> 00:00:14.319
Hello, hello, HELLO, my
friends! It's me — Buzzy!

2
00:00:14.519 --> 00:00:16.345
Welcome back to the garden!

3
00:00:19.545 --> 00:00:22.878
Oh, I saw that! What a lovely wave.

4
00:00:23.078 --> 00:00:27.987
Here's a big question. How do you
know what's happening around you?

5
00:00:32.207 --> 00:00:37.196
Lily! Just in time. How do
we find out about the world?

6
00:00:37.396 --> 00:00:40.989
Ooh. With my eyes? I look at things.

7
00:00:41.189 --> 00:00:45.599
Yes! And that's called a
sense. Your sense of sight.

8
00:00:45.799 --> 00:00:48.583
A sense? Is there more than one?

9
00:00:48.783 --> 00:00:52.579
There are five! Five
senses, Lily. And today,

10
00:00:52.599 --> 00:00:55.737
we're going to find every single one.

11
00:00:55.937 --> 00:00:58.981
Five! Let's go and find them!

12
00:01:02.181 --> 00:01:07.908
Five it is. Come on, everybody.
Let's have a sense-ational adventure!

13
00:01:11.378 --> 00:01:13.933
Here we are! Sense number one.

14
00:01:14.133 --> 00:01:18.253
Everybody, put your
hands over your eyes. Go on!

15
00:01:21.453 --> 00:01:23.439
Can you see anything at all?

16
00:01:23.639 --> 00:01:26.014
Not a thing! It's all dark.

17
00:01:26.214 --> 00:01:28.030
Now — open them up!

18
00:01:29.250 --> 00:01:31.595
Ta-daaa! Look at all this!

19
00:01:31.795 --> 00:01:33.502
Wow. The colours!

20
00:01:33.702 --> 00:01:39.029
That's your sense of SIGHT. Your
eyes let you see colours, and shapes,

21
00:01:39.049 --> 00:01:40.806
and how big things are.

22
00:01:41.006 --> 00:01:45.087
Let's practise. I'll say a
colour, and you find it.

23
00:01:45.287 --> 00:01:47.233
Can you find something RED?

24
00:01:50.433 --> 00:01:52.249
I found a red tulip!

25
00:01:52.449 --> 00:01:54.944
Beautiful. Now something YELLOW.

26
00:01:58.144 --> 00:02:00.379
The middle of the daisy is yellow!

27
00:02:00.579 --> 00:02:03.902
Now here's the tricky
one. Something GREEN.

28
00:02:07.102 --> 00:02:13.178
That's easy. The grass, the
leaves, the stems — green, green, green!

29
00:02:13.378 --> 00:02:18.267
Brilliant looking, everybody.
That's sense number one: seeing.

30
00:02:24.737 --> 00:02:26.364
Tweet! Tweet-tweet!

31
00:02:26.564 --> 00:02:28.650
Oh! Did you hear that?

32
00:02:28.850 --> 00:02:31.005
I did! Who was that?

33
00:02:31.205 --> 00:02:33.560
It was me! Hello, I'm Pip.

34
00:02:33.760 --> 00:02:36.554
Everybody, this is sense number two.

35
00:02:36.754 --> 00:02:40.905
Close your eyes for me.
Now — what can you hear?

36
00:02:44.305 --> 00:02:46.211
I can hear Pip singing!

37
00:02:46.411 --> 00:02:48.926
And the water going splish, splash.

38
00:02:49.126 --> 00:02:52.558
And the wind in the leaves. Shhhhhh.

39
00:02:52.758 --> 00:02:58.589
Open your eyes! That was your sense
of HEARING. Your ears did all of that,

40
00:02:58.609 --> 00:03:00.032
all by themselves.

41
00:03:00.232 --> 00:03:04.852
My ears were working the whole
time and I didn't even know!

42
00:03:06.072 --> 00:03:11.320
Now, listen very carefully. Is
this sound LOUD, or is it QUIET?

43
00:03:14.520 --> 00:03:17.593
Quiet! Well listened. And this one?

44
00:03:20.793 --> 00:03:22.470
That one made me jump!

45
00:03:22.670 --> 00:03:26.511
Let's make a sound
together! Can you clap your hands?

46
00:03:31.211 --> 00:03:35.771
What a wonderful noise.
That's sense number two: hearing.

47
00:03:43.141 --> 00:03:47.512
Mmmmm. Oh, my
goodness. Come and smell this.

48
00:03:47.712 --> 00:03:48.590
What is it?

49
00:03:48.790 --> 00:03:52.572
It's the flower. Take a big
breath in through your nose.

50
00:03:57.892 --> 00:04:00.905
Ohhh! It's sweet! Like honey!

51
00:04:01.105 --> 00:04:05.835
That's sense number three.
SMELLING. Your nose is doing that.

52
00:04:06.035 --> 00:04:10.296
Some smells are lovely. And
some are... not so lovely.

53
00:04:11.416 --> 00:04:14.758
Ugh! Has anybody been
near the compost heap?

54
00:04:14.958 --> 00:04:18.221
Oh dear. Dotty found
a not-so-lovely one.

55
00:04:21.621 --> 00:04:24.794
Mine is bread. Warm bread from the oven.

56
00:04:24.994 --> 00:04:28.546
And mine is flowers,
of course. I'm a bee!

57
00:04:28.746 --> 00:04:32.708
Three senses found.
Seeing, hearing, and smelling.

58
00:04:38.278 --> 00:04:41.201
Now this one — this one is my favourite.

59
00:04:41.401 --> 00:04:43.527
What's in the basket, Buzzy?

60
00:04:44.747 --> 00:04:45.755
A strawberry!

61
00:04:45.955 --> 00:04:49.038
Take a little taste. Just a little one.

62
00:04:50.258 --> 00:04:52.414
Mmmm! It's SWEET!

63
00:04:52.614 --> 00:04:58.840
Sense number four. TASTING. Your
tongue knows sweet, and salty, and sour.

64
00:04:59.040 --> 00:05:00.766
Sour? What's sour?

65
00:05:00.966 --> 00:05:03.1000
Oh, Dotty. You're going to find out.

66
00:05:05.120 --> 00:05:07.485
It's yellow. It looks lovely.

67
00:05:11.705 --> 00:05:13.631
Oooooooh! That's SOUR!

68
00:05:13.831 --> 00:05:17.712
And remember — we only
taste things we know are safe.

69
00:05:17.912 --> 00:05:20.157
Always ask a grown-up first!

70
00:05:20.357 --> 00:05:22.822
Exactly right. That's four!

71
00:05:29.292 --> 00:05:31.876
One more to find. Just one!

72
00:05:32.076 --> 00:05:34.551
The last sense! What is it?

73
00:05:35.771 --> 00:05:39.333
Feel this moss. Go
on, reach out with me.

74
00:05:42.733 --> 00:05:45.637
It's soft! Like a little cushion.

75
00:05:45.837 --> 00:05:50.447
That's sense number five.
TOUCHING. And your skin does it.

76
00:05:51.567 --> 00:05:54.301
Ooh! This one isn't soft at all!

77
00:05:54.501 --> 00:05:56.806
What does it feel like, Dotty?

78
00:05:57.006 --> 00:05:59.092
Bumpy. And a bit prickly.

79
00:05:59.292 --> 00:06:02.215
Bumpy and prickly. Lovely describing.

80
00:06:03.435 --> 00:06:06.389
And this rock is smooth. And cold!

81
00:06:06.589 --> 00:06:12.695
Smooth. Cold. Rough. Warm.
Soft. Your skin knows them all.

82
00:06:16.095 --> 00:06:19.219
Mine is fuzzy! I'm a bee, remember.

83
00:06:19.419 --> 00:06:22.512
And that's five! We found all five!

84
00:06:25.082 --> 00:06:28.425
We did it! Let's
count them all together.

85
00:06:28.625 --> 00:06:31.159
Number one — my eyes can SEE.

86
00:06:34.359 --> 00:06:36.974
Number two — my ears can HEAR.

87
00:06:40.174 --> 00:06:43.526
My nose can SMELL, and
my tongue can TASTE.

88
00:06:46.726 --> 00:06:49.690
And number five — my skin can TOUCH.

89
00:06:52.890 --> 00:06:55.564
Five senses! Let's sing it!

90
00:06:55.764 --> 00:06:58.149
Sing along with me, everybody!

91
00:07:02.849 --> 00:07:05.274
Eyes to see and ears to hear,

92
00:07:05.474 --> 00:07:07.949
A nose to smell the flowers near,

93
00:07:08.149 --> 00:07:10.823
A tongue to taste our lunch today,

94
00:07:11.023 --> 00:07:13.338
And skin to feel along the way!

95
00:07:13.538 --> 00:07:17.868
Five senses, five senses,
one two three four five!

96
00:07:18.068 --> 00:07:22.628
Five senses, five senses,
they help us feel alive!

97
00:07:24.748 --> 00:07:27.901
So next time you're outside, have a go.

98
00:07:28.101 --> 00:07:30.955
What can you see? What can you hear?

99
00:07:31.155 --> 00:07:34.099
What can you smell,
and what can you touch?

100
00:07:34.299 --> 00:07:37.721
Thank you for coming on
our sense-ational adventure!

101
00:07:37.921 --> 00:07:41.623
I'll see you next
time. Bye bye, friends!

